<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ ni_server_name }} — CTTB PXE / Network Install</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="fonts.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="citylights.min.css">
<style>
.chain-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 0 .8em;
}
@media (max-width: 800px) {
  .chain-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
.chain-grid fieldset { margin: 0 0 1em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="site-title">
    <h1><span>{{ ni_server_name | regex_replace('\\.cttb$', '') }}</span>.cttb</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">PXE / Network Install Server — City of Ten Thousand Buddhas</p>
  </div>
  <div class="meta">
    <span><span class="dot">&#x25CF;</span> {{ ansible_default_ipv4.address | default('—') }}</span>
    <span>{{ ansible_distribution | default('Linux') }} {{ ansible_distribution_version | default('') }}</span>
    <span>{{ ansible_hostname | default('pxe') }}</span>
  </div>
</header>

<main>

<p class="notice">
  <strong>Internal resource.</strong> This server delivers PXE boot
  files, kernels, initrd images, autoinstall configs, and ISO images
  to lab machines on the CTTB campus. Intended for use by IT staff
  and infrastructure clients only.
</p>

<article class="content-area">

<fieldset class="file-group">
  <legend>☸ Message</legend>
  <p>
    A PXE server is the network's <em>bīja</em> — the seed-bank from which a
    bare machine ripens into a working host. Every Sudhanix install on this
    campus has its origin here: kernel, initrd, autoinstall recipe, and
    finally a freshly-provisioned desktop or server.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>{{ ni_server_name }}</strong> serves the modern Ubuntu / Debian
    network-install pipeline (subiquity / cloud-init autoinstall over HTTP +
    GRUB EFI / PXELINUX over TFTP). Browse the served tree under
    <a href="/netinstall/">/netinstall/</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Boot options</strong> — default <strong>{{ ni_pxe_default }}</strong> after
    {{ (ni_pxe_timeout / 10) | int }} s (BIOS) / {{ ni_grub_timeout }} s (UEFI):
    an unattended PXE boot falls through to the local disk. Reimaging is opt-in
    per MAC, or armed deliberately with
    <code>-e ni_pxe_default=&lt;LABEL&gt; -t ni_pxe_menu</code>.
  </p>
  <div class="quick-ref">
{% for img in ni_2404_images %}
{% for ai in img.autoinstall %}
    <p><code>Autoinstall-{{ img.name }}-{{ ai.name }}</code> — {{ ai.description }} ({{ img.os }} {{ img.type }} {{ img.arch }})</p>
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
    <p><code>BootLocal</code> — boot the local disk (default) · <code>Memtest</code> — memory test (BIOS menu only)</p>
    <p>Menu fragments live in <code>{{ ni_pxe_menu_dir }}/</code> (<a href="/netinstall/menu/">browse</a>); rendered by the <code>netinstall-2404</code> role (<code>-t ni_pxe_menu</code>)</p>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset class="file-group">
  <legend>Network Install Tree <a href="/netinstall/">[browse]</a></legend>
  <p>
    Kernels, initrd, ISOs, autoinstall <code>user-data</code> /
    <code>meta-data</code>, PXE menu fragments, and the
    <code>pxelinux.cfg/default</code> rendered by the
    <code>netinstall-2404</code> Ansible role.
  </p>
  <div class="icon-grid">
    <a href="/netinstall/" class="icon-tile"><span class="icon">📂</span><span class="name">Browse netinstall/</span></a>
    <a href="/netinstall/autoinstall/" class="icon-tile"><span class="icon">📜</span><span class="name">autoinstall configs</span></a>
    <a href="/netinstall/menu/" class="icon-tile"><span class="icon">📋</span><span class="name">PXE menu fragments</span></a>
    <a href="/netinstall/pxelinux.cfg/" class="icon-tile"><span class="icon">🧭</span><span class="name">pxelinux.cfg</span></a>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<div class="chain-grid">

<fieldset class="file-group">
  <legend>BIOS Boot Chain <a href="/netinstall/pxelinux.cfg/">[pxelinux.cfg]</a></legend>
  <p>
    Legacy-firmware clients chain: DHCP → <code>pxelinux.0</code> over TFTP →
    <code>menu.c32</code> → the shared menu in <code>pxelinux.cfg/default</code>.
    Per-machine one-shot overrides go in <code>pxelinux.cfg/01-&lt;mac&gt;</code>.
  </p>
  <div class="quick-ref">
    <p><code>{{ ni_tftp_dir }}/pxelinux.0</code> — BIOS boot loader (<code>tftp://{{ ni_server_name }}/pxelinux.0</code>)</p>
    <p><code>{{ ni_tftp_dir }}/pxelinux.cfg/default</code> — BIOS menu config (<a href="/netinstall/pxelinux.cfg/default">view</a>)</p>
    <p><code>{{ ni_tftp_dir }}/ldlinux.c32</code>, <code>menu.c32</code>, <code>libcom32.c32</code> — syslinux modules beside the loader</p>
  </div>
</fieldset>

<fieldset class="file-group">
  <legend>UEFI Boot Chain <a href="/netinstall/grub/">[grub]</a></legend>
  <p>
    UEFI clients chain: DHCP → <code>grubx64.efi</code> over TFTP →
    <code>grub/grub.cfg</code>. There is no shim hop — shim 15.8 mis-derives its
    netboot second stage (rhboot/shim#696), so dnsmasq points firmware straight
    at GRUB and Secure Boot stays off on clients for the install.
    <code>shimx64.efi</code> is staged for the day a fixed signed shim exists.
  </p>
  <div class="quick-ref">
    <p><code>{{ ni_tftp_dir }}/grubx64.efi</code> — signed GRUB netboot build, prefix <code>/grub</code> (<code>tftp://{{ ni_server_name }}/grubx64.efi</code>)</p>
    <p><code>{{ ni_tftp_dir }}/grub/grub.cfg</code> — UEFI menu config (<a href="/netinstall/grub/grub.cfg">view</a>)</p>
  </div>
</fieldset>

</div><!-- /chain-grid -->

<fieldset class="file-group">
  <legend>Endpoints</legend>
  <p>Quick references for cutover scripts and clients:</p>
  <div class="quick-ref">
    <p><code>http://{{ ni_server_name }}/healthz</code> — liveness probe (200 ok)</p>
    <p><code>http://{{ ni_server_name }}/netinstall/</code> — browseable index</p>
    <p><code>tftp://{{ ni_server_name }}/pxelinux.0</code> — TFTP boot loader</p>
  </div>
</fieldset>

</article>

</main>

<footer>
  <p>
    CTTB IT — Managed via <a href="http://wiki.cttb/wiki/IT:Ansible">Ansible</a>
    — Container <code>{{ ansible_hostname | default('pxe24') }}</code> on <code>srv-nas</code> (10.11.1.5)
    <br>Made with ❤️ by <a href="https://github.com/moonexpr/">jc</a>
  </p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
